; isort-perm.elab — insertion sort produces a PERMUTATION of its input (the multiset/count half of full sort
; correctness): forall l y. count(isort l, y) = count(l, y) [count = number of occurrences of y]. With isort-sorted
; and isort-preserves-length, this gives FULL insertion-sort correctness: isort produces a SORTED PERMUTATION.
; count uses decidable nat-equality nateq (dual dispatch) and addIfEq(bool,n)=if bool then s n else n. Crux helper
; cpisort = count-preserved-by-insert (count(insert(l,x),y)=count(Cons x l,y)), whose append case reduces to
; addIfEqCommute (the two occurrence-increments commute). Then induction on l applying cpisort at (isort t, h).
